# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: the WebP plug-in, from LumenWebP-<ver>.zip.
Package: LumenWebP
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: Lumen (>= 0.0.38), SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Description: WebP pictures for Lumen (libwebp)
 Lets Lumen import, show, adjust and export WebP pictures, lossy and
 lossless, with or without transparency, and the first frame of animated
 ones, with Google's libwebp 1.6.0, and reads their EXIF (camera, date
 and where they were taken). It uses NEON where the computer has it. It
 needs about 40 MB of memory to decode a 12 megapixel picture. It goes
 into Lumen's Plugins directory; Lumen finds it the next time it starts.
Build-Map: !Lumen/Plugins/WebP -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen/Plugins/WebP
Build-Notice: The WebP plug-in for Lumen, packaged for PackMan from its
 release zip.
